+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates model-supplied tool inputs against each registered tool's declared JSON Schema `inputSchema` before the executor runs. Schema violations return an actionable rejection `ToolResponse` so the orchestrator can feed the error back to the model for self-correction, while unknown tool names continue to throw.
+
+## Input validation at execution
+
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with input missing a `required` field returns a `ToolResponse` naming the missing field as required without invoking the executor ([validated by: returns a rejection ToolResponse naming missing required fields before running the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L25)).
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with a wrong-typed field or an invalid `enum` value returns a rejection naming the failing field path and expected constraint without invoking the executor, and neither the returned `result` nor any log line contains offending or identifying input values ([validated by: rejects type and enum violations without leaking offending or identifying values in results or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults — so a rejected tool call in `ChatOrchestrator` feeds the error text back to the model on the next round and valid input with unlisted properties passes through unmodified ([validated by: feeds validation rejections back to the model for retry and passes valid input with extra fields unmodified](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L147)).
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` for an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+## Schema compilation and dynamic definitions
+
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool's `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool if the schema cannot compile ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when its inputSchema cannot compile](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
+- A static tool's compiled validator is cached at registration time and reused across repeated `execute` calls rather than recompiled per call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call and validates against the schema current at that call rather than a stale cached validator ([validated by: re-validates a function-valued tool definition against the current schema on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L106)).
